## Quality Check Rules

**All quality verification is done locally. CI is for build confirmation only.**

### Flow

```
Harness-only diff? -> skip quality-check entirely (the gate exempts it;
                      gate-parameter changes are NOT exempt - see Quality Check Hook)
    |
Step 1: Change area + risk level detection (git diff; risk levels per quality policy §1)
    |
Step 2/3: Static checks + tests (High/Medium: cross-check the test-design memo)
    |
Step 4: Review cycles (staged personas by diff size, min 1 cycle; cycles 2+ verify fixes
        with only the personas that raised findings; a new high finding reverts to the
        full set; the QA persona works falsification-first)
    |
Step 5: Additional-test proposal (test-recommendation skill: heuristics recommend
        mutation/E2E runs with rationale, the user decides, approved runs execute;
        declines are recorded and never block - except an executed E2E that fails
        must be fixed)
    |
Step 6: Report data saved -> .quality-check-passed (commit-bound JSON) created -> merge allowed
```

Thresholds, cycle caps and time budgets are defined in `documents/development/quality-policy.md` (§1 risk levels, §2 gate matrix, §5 loop protection). Do not restate the numbers here - read them from the policy.

### Quality Check Hook

Codex enforces this via a `PreToolUse` hook (configured in `.codex/hooks.json`).
When you run `gh pr merge`, `git merge` on main, or push to main, Codex validates `.quality-check-passed` (commit-bound JSON: `{branch, commit}`). **Pushes to feature branches are not gated.** The flag is not consumed; it stays valid while post-check commits touch only harness files (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursorrules`, `.claude/**`, `.codex/**`, `.cursor/**`, `skills/project/**`, `skills/superpowers/**`, `.github/review-*.md`, `documents/development/coding-rules/**`). Exception: a post-check commit that touches gate control-plane files (listed below) DOES invalidate the flag - the hook blocks with `Gate control-plane changed:` and quality-check must be re-run. Harness-only diffs skip the gate and the quality check entirely. **Carve-out**: a diff that changes gate parameters - the `Quality Gate Overrides` keys below - is NOT exempt, even inside those paths. It must go through quality-check (a reduced-persona review at minimum). The same applies to **gate control-plane files** - `skills/project/quality-check/**` and `skills/project/_schemas/**`, the `.claude/skills` and `.claude/hooks` trees (including the `.claude/skills` symlink node itself - `init` creates it as a link, and re-pointing that one path swaps the whole quality-check tree) and their `.codex/**` / `.cursor/**` copies, `.github/review-*.md`, the hook registration files (`.codex/hooks.json` and the `.claude` / `.cursor` equivalents), `.codex/config.toml` (whole-file: it can carry an inline `[hooks]` table, a `[features]` hooks kill-switch and `[[rules]]` deny decisions), the MCP registration files (`.claude/mcp.json` / `.codex/mcp.json` / `.cursor/mcp.json` - MCP server definitions register command execution, the same class as hooks), and the hook registration inside `.claude/settings.json` AND `.claude/settings.local.json` (Claude Code reads both, the latter at higher precedence): the `hooks` block, the `disableAllHooks` / `allowManagedHooksOnly` hook-disable keys, and the `permissions.deny` rule list (the deny layer backing the destructive-command guards; `permissions.allow` changes stay exempt) - unregistering or disabling the hook, or weakening the deny layer, disables protection just as surely as editing the hook does. Path matching is case-insensitive (`.claude/Hooks/...` is the same file as `.claude/hooks/...` on Windows/macOS). With in-development reviews consolidated into the merge gate, these must never change with zero review (the quality-gate hook enforces this carve-out and blocks such diffs with `Gate control-plane changed:`). If main advanced independently after the flag was issued, the merged main is unverified - re-run quality-check on it before pushing.

