### Multi-Persona Review

`quality-check` owns a single outer cycle (Step 2 static checks -> Step 3 tests -> Step 4 personas -> consolidated-findings fixes). Within Step 4, specialist personas review in parallel (each spawned with `gpt-5.6-sol` / `model_reasoning_effort = "high"` - see Subagent Model Selection):

| Persona | Focus Area |
|---------|------------|
| Security Engineer | Vulnerabilities, auth, data leaks, injection |
| Software Architect | SOLID/DRY, layer responsibilities, dependencies, extensibility |
| QA Engineer | Edge cases, test coverage, error handling |
| Integration Architecture | Overall consistency, layer dependencies, existing patterns, side effects |
| Performance Engineer | Algorithmic complexity, query performance, bundle size, caching |
| Requirements Consistency Reviewer | Issue/design alignment, acceptance criteria, domain terminology |

- **Completion criteria**: no High/Medium findings remaining in the consolidated results, minimum 1 cycle, and the Step 5 additional-test proposal presented with the user's decision recorded (the `quality-check` skill holds the full definition - read it there)
- Code changes under 200 diff lines (generated files excluded): 3 personas (Security, QA, Integration Architecture). 200+ lines: all 6 personas. Docs/infra-only changes: reduced persona set (see `quality-check` skill)
- Minimum 1 cycle. Run another cycle only if the previous one left High/Medium consolidated findings
- Cycles 2+ are a verification review: only the personas that raised High/Medium findings in the previous cycle re-review the fix diffs and responses; a new high finding reverts the next cycle to the full persona set over the full diff
- Run `self-improvement` before creating `.quality-check-passed`

